@startuml
' Figure 3.4 - Sequence Diagram, Order Submission and Recipe Deduction
'
' Rebuilt in PlantUML. The mermaid version could not be sized: mermaid 11 ignores
' sequence options from both a %%{init}%% directive and mmdc -c, so actorMargin,
' messageMargin and every font size were inert - it rendered at a fixed 16px in a
' 1863-unit viewBox, which is 3.6pt on the page. PlantUML honours them.
'
' One colour per participant, as in the original figure.
'
' Sizing: printed size is fontSize x 668.2 / canvas_width when the figure is placed
' landscape, so canvas WIDTH is the only thing that matters. Width is the sum of the
' eight columns, and each column is as wide as its widest label - so participant names
' and message labels are kept short and the detail is carried in notes, which are
' anchored "over" a pair of lifelines and therefore cannot widen the canvas.
'
' Verified against OrderService.submitOrder, RecipeDeductionService.deductForOrder /
' handlePostDeductionThresholds and InventoryAlertService.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Arial"
skinparam defaultFontSize 26
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.8

skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #37474F
  ArrowFontSize 25
  ParticipantFontSize 26
  ParticipantFontStyle bold
  ParticipantPadding 16
  BoxPadding 12
  LifeLineBorderColor #90A4AE
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  GroupHeaderFontSize 25
  GroupHeaderFontStyle bold
  GroupBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
  GroupBorderColor #2E7D32
}
skinparam note {
  FontSize 23
  BackgroundColor #FFF8E1
  BorderColor #F9A825
}

hide footbox

title Sequence Diagram — Order Submission and Recipe Deduction Engine

participant "Waiter\n(POS UI)"   as W  #BBDEFB
participant "Order\nController"  as C  #E3F2FD
participant "Order\nService"     as OS #C8E6C9
participant "Recipe\nDeduction"  as RD #FFE0B2
participant "Ingredient\nRepo"   as IR #FFCDD2
participant "Inventory\nLedger"  as IL #E1BEE7
participant "Event\nPublisher"   as EP #DCEDC8
participant "Inventory\nAlert"   as AL #FFCCBC

W  -> C  : 1. POST /api/orders
C  -> OS : 2. submitOrder\n(request,\nwaiterPrincipal)

group Single @Transactional boundary — steps 3 to 19
  OS -> OS : 3. tableService.\nopenTableForOrder
  note over OS, RD
    SELECT … FOR UPDATE
    on the table row —
    status becomes OCCUPIED
  end note
  OS -> OS : 4. customer\nRepository.\nfindByPhoneNumber
  note over OS, RD
    creates a Walk-in customer if unknown
  end note
  OS -> OS : 5. menuItem\nRepository.\nfindById per line
  note over OS, RD
    an unavailable item is rejected
  end note

  OS -> RD : 6. deductForOrder(lines)
  note over OS, RD
    @Transactional(REQUIRED) —
    joins the caller's transaction
  end note
  RD -> RD : 7. recipe\nRepository.\nfindByMenuItemId
  note over RD, IL
    summed per ingredient across the order
  end note
  RD -> IR : 8. findAllById\nForUpdate\n(sorted ids)
  note over RD, IL
    SELECT … FOR UPDATE in ascending id order
    — blocks concurrent transactions,
    avoids deadlock
  end note
  IR --> RD : 9. locked Ingredient rows
  RD -> RD : 10. validate stock\n≥ required qty
  note over RD, IL #FFCDD2
    any shortfall raises InsufficientStockException
    → HTTP 409 and the whole transaction
    rolls back
  end note
  RD -> RD : 11a. newStock =\ncurrent −\n(qty × recipeQty)
  RD -> IR : 11b. save(ingredient)
  RD -> IL : 12. recordRecipeDeduction
  IL --> RD : 13. ledger row appended
  RD -> EP : 14. publishMenuItem\nAvailabilityChanged
  note over EP, AL
    only when stock reached zero
  end note
  RD -> RD : 15. publishEvent\n(ReorderThreshold\nBreachedEvent)
  RD --> OS : 16. deduction complete
  OS -> OS : 17. orderRepository\n.save(order)\n— PENDING
  OS -> EP : 18. publishNewTicket
  OS -> EP : 19. publishTable\nStatusChanged
end

note over OS, EP #E8F5E9
  Transaction commits on return. Steps 18 and 19
  are dispatched inside it — the stock alert below
  is deferred to AFTER_COMMIT.
end note

EP --> W : 20. STOMP → /topic/kitchen\nand /topic/tables
OS --> C : 21. OrderResponse\n(id, status)
C  --> W : 22. 201 Created

AL -> AL : 23. onReorder\nThresholdBreached\n(event)
note over EP, AL
  @Async @TransactionalEventListener(AFTER_COMMIT)
  — own thread, once the order has committed
end note
AL -> AL : 24. handleReorder\nBreach(ingredientId,\nseverity)
note over EP, AL
  drafts a Purchase Order if none is in flight
end note
AL -> EP : 25. publishStockAlert

@enduml
